title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf metarecord add
catalog: CLI command
target: mf metarecord add
summary: Create a metarecord with the given fields and print its UUID (no selector)

!! Reference

```
Create a metarecord with the given fields and print its UUID (no selector)

Usage: mf metarecord add [OPTIONS] [SPECS]...

Arguments:
  [SPECS]...
          Field spec name:type[=value]; repeatable

Options:
  -f, --force
          Required to write mfr_* fields

      --path <PATH>
          The metarecord of this existing file or directory: its mfr_* fields are read from disk, and it gets mf_watch = false (recorded, not followed) unless a spec sets mf_watch. Refused if the path already has one (`mf uuid` finds it)

      --parents
          With --path: also create the metarecords of the parent directories that have none (refused otherwise, listing them)

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
